    "text": {
     "en": "Ashoka ruled the Mauryan Empire from about 268 BCE. He won the Kalinga war but was troubled by the loss of life.\nHe followed Buddhism and spread Dhamma, a way of living with kindness, tolerance, truthfulness and respect for all.\nHe built roads, rest houses, hospitals and planted trees, and had his messages carved on rocks and pillars called edicts."
    }
